]

data emit_host_node_smoke_subject_note: String = "run_node_http_serve_smoke joins the ECMASCRIPT subject, not TypeScript, and the distinction is the point. The smoke writes a server.js heredoc and executes it with node; DESIGN describes the same artifact as 'an emitted-JS static server'. So the LANGUAGE OF THE ARTIFACT is JavaScript. Two things this row deliberately does NOT claim: Node.js is the RUNTIME, an independently governed upstream product that would take its own subject if it were ever registered as a target, so it is not fused into this language identity; and this is not evidence that the v2.extdeps.languages.ecmascript MODULE has consumers — measured 2026-08-04, that module still has zero importers anywhere in the tree, exactly as the legacy frontier table says. A surface emitting a language is a different fact from a module being imported, and only the first is what this census row records."

